br>Military governors established by Hsuan-tsung (712-756 CE) in frontier areas. <br>Maintained about 600 militia units of between 800-1,200 men. "While the Sui had subordinated these units to the local civil administration, the T\'ang controlled them centrally, via a bureaucracy answerable to the ping-pu or Ministry of the Army. Units contained both cavalry and infantry, and were subdivided into t\'uan of 200 men, tui of 50, and huo of 10." <br>"Many of the peasants in areas of strategic importance were also obliged to serve in militia units for a specified period of time - usually one month in five. There were approximately 630 militia units, each of them theoretically composed of 1000 men. This system prevailed until almost the middle of the 8th century when it disintegrated, for a number of reasons, and was replaced by a standing army." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2871, 'temperature': 0.2})
